    "lyrics": [],
    "notes": "Two parts (Flute, Tuba), C major, 16 bars.  Pitches in the truth are SOUNDING pitches; 8va / 8vb brackets are <octave-shift> directions (type down = 8va, type up = 8vb, MusicXML convention).  Flute reaches D7 (6 ledger lines when written at pitch, bars 2, 7, 15); bars 5-6 and 7-8 are the same music with and without 8va; bar 9 starts 8va on beat 2; bar 10 has C7 under 8va then C6 loco (same staff position, different octave); bars 11-13 8va crosses the line break.  Tuba goes down to C1 (5 ledger lines below the bass staff, bars 7, 16); 8vb (bars 5-6, 9-10, 12-13, the last across a line break).  A correct conversion must output the sounding octave for every note under a bracket and must NOT apply a bracket to notes after it ends.  Pencil marks (circles, breath marks, words) in the scans are not part of the music.  The scans are cropped through the left/right ends of the staves (instrument names, brackets and the final barline ends are cut; no notes are cut)."
  },
